  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 36,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Machine being measured",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "These metrics describe the **Docker host** \u2014 the laptop or VM running `docker compose` \u2014 labelled `machine=\"docker-host\"`, `job=\"node-exporter\"`.\n\nnode-exporter runs in the host's own network, PID and filesystem namespaces (`network_mode: host`, `pid: host`, with `/proc`, `/sys` and `/` bind-mounted read-only), so it reports the machine's real counters rather than the container's. Every container in this stack is a process on this kernel, so their CPU and memory use is included in these totals.\n\nHostname: `{{ instance }}` \u2014 see the **Instance** column in any panel legend."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 37,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "CPU",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 38,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "CPU busy",
      "description": "node_cpu_seconds_total is a COUNTER of seconds each core spent in each mode. There is no 'CPU %' metric: the percentage is derived as 1 minus the idle rate, averaged over the cores.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "1 - avg(rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{mode=\"idle\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "busy",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 2,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.75
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.9
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "graphMode": "area",
        "colorMode": "background",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 39,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Load (1m)",
      "description": "GAUGE. Runnable + uninterruptible processes. Compare against the core count: load above the core count means tasks are queueing.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 5
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "node_load1",
          "legendFormat": "load1",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 2,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
